he plains, Governors'' riverine classics","si":"ultra","blurb":"the Mara''s apex camps — Angama''s escarpment glass tents over the plains, Governors'' riverine classics","when":"standing; peak 6-12 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["romance","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"destination","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Mara honeymoon (escarpment / riverine)","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jul-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jul-Oct","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Maasai manyatta visit","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$20-50/pp","timing":"Jul-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the Maasai homeland the Mara is named for — a manyatta visit, the adumu jumping dance and beadwork, with a fair-trade, community-benefiting operator","si":"culture","blurb":"the Maasai homeland the Mara is named for — a manyatta visit, the adumu jumping dance and beadwork, with a fair-trade, community-benefiting operator","when":"Jul-Oct","commission":"DMC/community","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in the Maasai Mara?","a":"Dangerous game and remoteness, not the parks. Lions, elephants and buffalo are at close range - stay in the vehicle and follow your guide; at the crossings keep to designated vantage points (3,000+ crocodiles). Ground EMS is limited, so carry AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30 days, evac to Nairobi) + travel-medical insurance.","source":"flydoc.org","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit - migration or big cats?","a":"For the Great Migration and Mara River crossings, come Jul-Oct (peak Aug-Sep). For big cats without the migration crush, come Jan-Mar. The long rains (Apr-May) are lush, quiet and cheapest. Book 6-12 months ahead for the Jul-Oct peak.","source":"dumaexplorer.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Reserve or a conservancy - what''s the difference?","a":"The National Reserve has the classic crossings but more vehicles; the surrounding conservancies (community/private land) offer fewer vehicles, walking safaris, off-road and night drives - the more exclusive, often ultra, choice. Many itineraries combine both.","source":"masaimarareserve.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How much does a Maasai Mara safari cost?","a":"Reserve entry is $200/pp/day (2026 peak); a mid-range 4-day Mara safari runs ~$1,400-2,500/pp including the domestic flight, and a luxury 4-night peak stay $3,450-7,800/pp depending on camp.","source":"dumaexplorer.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Kenya?","a":"An eTA (Kenya replaced visas with the eTA in 2024 - apply at least 2 weeks ahead; required for all visitors). Yellow fever is compulsory only if you arrive from a YF-risk country (cert valid 10 days post-injection); CDC recommends the vaccine for most.","source":"en.wikipedia.org","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Maasai Mara Safari Guide: Great Migration, Big Cats, Conservancies, Cost & Best Time","meta_de