"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"balloon + conservancy walking/night drives"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future","note":"Maasai"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Angama Mara - the escarpment apex","why_ultra":"glass-fronted tented suites 300m above the Mara Triangle, private guiding, the migration below - a Virtuoso value-add stay","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,500-3,000+/night"},{"name":"A private conservancy mobile camp + private guide + balloon","why_ultra":"exclusive-use conservancy camp, private vehicle/guide with walking + night drives, the dawn balloon","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"A Mara + Serengeti cross-border migration week (private-guided)","why_ultra":"follow the herds across the ecosystem, Kenya + Tanzania luxury camps, private guiding (mind the YF-transit rule)","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-31","hero":{"query":"Maasai Mara National Reserve, Kenya"},"geo":{"lat":-1.5,"lng":35.15},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["amboseli-kenya","laikipia-kenya","samburu-kenya","tsavo-kenya"]}'::jsonb, 0),
  ('serengeti-tanzania', '05A', 'Serengeti National Park', 'Tanzania', 'The greatest wildlife show on Earth', 'live', 'verified', 'safariGiraffe', 'Tanzania — Northern Safari Circuit / Serengeti', '{"safari","ultra","romance","adventure","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["The safari demo STAR: UNESCO 1981, world''s highest concentration of large predators + Africa''s largest lion population; the Great Migration - ~2M wildebeest + ~300k zebra + ~900k Thomson''s gazelles on a ~1,000 km annual circuit","Migration clock: Ndutu calving Jan-Feb (~500k calves in 2-3 wks); Grumeti crossings Jun (western); Mara River crossings Jul-Oct peak Aug-Sep (northern/Kogatende); Sept = best balance","Best general game-viewing dry season late Jun-Oct; 3-5 days typical; ~$600-2,700+/pp/day by comfort; book 6-12 mo ahead for peak","LGBTQ+ targeting flagged); safari with a licensed operator - disclose + consent","Sold via safari DMCs - IATAN/host-gated NOT CLIA; commission ~10-20%; TANAPA park fees non-commissionable; AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) for remote evac","TZS (~2,633/USD) but USD is the safari currency; eVisa required; malaria prophylaxis recommended (lower risk at elevation); YF only if transiting a risk country (e.g. Kenya) >12h"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 999 (unreliable in remote areas - rely on camp/operator radio + AMREF Flying Doctors)","hospital":"Remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d, bush-airstrip evac; NOT hospital/repatriation) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Arusha","malaria":"prophylaxis recommended (CDC) - lower risk at 920-1,800m elevation but present; DEET + cover at dusk","yellow_fever":"not required from a non-risk country; mandatory if transiting >12h a risk country (e.g. Kenya)","activity_note":"LGBTQ+ targeting flagged). DANGEROUS-GAME country: stay in the vehicle except designated areas, follow the guide; walking safari armed-ranger only; balloon TCAA-inspected; remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-09-01T16:20:26Z","page_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00","source_country":"tanzania","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jul-Oct (dry + Mara River crossings, Aug-Sep drama); secondary Jan-Feb (Ndutu calving)","shoulder":"Jun (Grumeti crossings, less crowded) + Nov (short rains, herds moving south)","green":"Mar-May (long rains - lush, quiet, cheapest; some camps close)","booking_lead":"6-12 mo for Jul-Sep peak + calving (premium/mobile camps sell out); mid-range 3-6 mo; green 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"Mar-May green-season value + Grumeti-crossing (Jun) shoulder; combine Ngorongoro/Tarangire","event_peaks":"Jul-Sep Mara-crossing crush + Jan-Feb calving; Christmas/NY + Easter; N-Hemisphere summer","fire_date":"Jul-Sep crossings 9-12 mo out (by prior Oct-Dec); Jan-Feb calving by prior Apr-Jun; green-season value by prior Nov-Dec"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Great Migration - Mara River crossings","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$1,200-2,700+/pp/day","timing":"Jul-Oct; book 9-12 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the planet''s greatest overland migration at its most dramatic — herds massing and plunging past waiting crocodiles in the northern Serengeti, Jul–Oct, peak Aug–Sep","si":"safari","blurb":"the planet''s greatest overland migration at its most dramatic — herds massing and plunging past waiting crocodiles in the northern Serengeti, Jul–Oct, peak Aug–Sep","when":"Jul-Oct; book 9-12 mo","commission":"safari DMC 10-20%","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane","source":"https://savannasojourns.com/great-wildebeest-migration-2026-when-where-to-see-the-mara-river-crossings/","accessed":"2026-07-31","source_carried":true,"source_basis":"carried from the dossier lane source; the proper noun ''Mara River'' from the jewel name appears in the URL. NOT a human read of the jewel."},{"name":"The Ndutu calving","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$1,000-2,500/pp/day","timing":"Jan-Feb; book 6-9 mo","draw_rank":2,"hook":"~500,000 calves born in a 2–3-week window in the southern Ndutu plains — concentrated big-cat action","si":"safari","blurb":"~500,000 calves born in a 2–3-week window in the southern Ndutu plains — concentrated big-cat action","when":"Jan-Feb; book 6-9 mo","commission":"safari DMC 10-20%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — commission lane ''safari dmc 10-20%''","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Big-cat & Big Five game drives (Seronera)","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~$600-1,800/pp/day","timing":"year-round; dry Jun-Oct best","draw_rank":3,"hook":"the highest predator density on Earth — lion prides, cheetah on the plains, leopard in the kopjes","si":"safari","blurb":"the highest predator density on Earth — lion prides, cheetah on the plains, leopard in the kopjes","when":"year-round; dry Jun-Oct best","commission":"safari DMC 10-20%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — commission lane ''safari dmc 10-20%''","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"The Grumeti crossings (Western Corridor)","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$1,000-2,200/pp/day","timing":"Jun","draw_rank":4,"hook":"June''s first major crossings on the Grumeti — less famous, less crowded, equally wild — a shoulder-season alternative to the Mara crush","si":"safari","blurb":"June''s first major crossings on the Grumeti — less famous, less crowded, equally wild — a shoulder-season alternative to the Mara crush","when":"Jun","commission":"safari DMC 10-20%","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Dawn hot-air balloon safari + bush breakfast","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$550-650/pp","timing":"Jul-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the signature Serengeti moment — sunrise over the plains from a balloon, then a champagne bush breakfast; TCAA-inspected operators","si":"adventure","blurb":"the signature Serengeti moment — sunrise over the plains from a balloon, then a champagne bush breakfast; TCAA-inspected operators","when":"Jul-Oct","commission":"DMC/camp 10-15%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","culture":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Guided walking safari (armed ranger)","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$100-200/pp","timing":"Jul-Oct","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the Serengeti on foot — tracks, dung, birdsong and the adrenaline of dangerous-game country with an armed ranger","si":"adventure","blurb":"the Serengeti on foot — tracks, dung, birdsong and the adrenaline of dangerous-game country with an armed ranger","when":"Jul-Oct","commission":"camp/DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","culture":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A migration-following luxury mobile camp","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$1,500-4,000+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 9-12 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the ultra way to do the migration — Singita, &Beyond, Nomad and Namiri Plains move their tented camps to the herds","si":"ultra","blurb":"the ultra way to do the migration — Singita, &Beyond, Nomad and Namiri Plains move their tented camps to the herds","when":"standing; peak 9-12 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["glamping","romance","safari","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_basis":"the dossier''s own SI block filed this jewel under a heading resolving to ''romance'' via ruled RULES. Not a keyword match on the jewel text. | added glamping 2026-10-05 - a luxury mobile tented camp"},{"name":"Honeymoon safari - star bed + bush dinner","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jul-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sundowners on the plains, a private bush dinner under the lanterns, a sleep-out under the Milky Way — the romance of the wild","si":"romance","blurb":"sundowners on the plains, a private bush dinner under the lanterns, a sleep-out under the Milky Way — the romance of the wild","when":"Jul-Oct","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay","eat","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Maasai cultural visit","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$20-60/pp","timing":"Jul-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the pastoralist Maasai of the Serengeti–Ngorongoro edge — a visit to a boma, the dances and the beadwork, done with a respectful, fair-trade operator","si":"culture","blurb":"the pastoralist Maasai of the Serengeti–Ngorongoro edge — a visit to a boma, the dances and the beadwork, done with a respectful, fair-trade operator","when":"Jul-Oct","commission":"DMC/community","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on a Serengeti safari?","a":"Not the parks - remoteness and wildlife discipline. Big game is genuinely dangerous: stay in the vehicle except in designated areas and follow your guide. The Serengeti is remote, so pair travel-medical insurance with AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30 days) for bush-airstrip evacuation. City petty crime, not park danger, is the everyday risk.","source":"flydoc.org","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Should LGBTQ+ travelers be aware of anything in Tanzania?","a":"Yes, plainly: Tanzanian law criminalizes same-sex relations and the US advisory specifically flags targeting of LGBTQ+ travelers. It''s a real safety consideration to weigh; discretion is advised, and we''ll talk it through candidly before you book.","source":"newsweek.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to see the Great Migration?","a":"General game-viewing is best in the dry season (late Jun-Oct). For the Mara River crossings, come Jul-Oct (peak Aug-Sep); for calving and big-cat drama, come Jan-Feb to the southern Ndutu plains. September is the best all-round balance of action and lighter crowds.","source":"dumaexplorer.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How many days do I need and what does a Serengeti safari cost?","a":"Plan 3-5 days (often combined with Ngorongoro/Tarangire). All-in cost runs roughly $600-1,000/day budget, $1,200-1,500 mid-range, $1,400-2,700+ luxury per person; book 6-12 months ahead for the Jul-Sep peak - premium camps sell out.","source":"bucketlistly.blog","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for the Serengeti?","a":"A visa (eVisa) - apply on the official Tanzania portal before departure (~2-10 days). Yellow fever isn''t required arriving directly from the US/Europe, but becomes mandatory if you transit >12h through a risk country like Kenya - key for Kenya-Tanzania combos.","source":"tanzania-specialist.com","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_description":"Plan a Serengeti safari - the Great Migration (~2M wildebeest), the Mara River crossings (Jul-Oct) and Ndutu calving (Jan-Feb), the highest big-cat density on Earth, dawn balloon flights and luxury migration camps - with real timing, cost, the FCDO advisory, malaria and evac intel.","slug":"serengeti-tanzania","primary_keyword":"Serengeti safari","long_tail":["Great Migration Serengeti 2026","Mara River crossings best time","Ndutu calving season","Serengeti balloon safari","is the Serengeti safe","Serengeti safari cost","best time to visit Serengeti"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Serengeti","Uhamiaji Mkubwa","Mto Mara","Ndutu","pundamilia","nyumbu","simba","safari ya puto"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-31","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-31","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:17Z","source_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["reconsider-travel","terrorism-mtwara","crime","lgbtq-targeting"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Serengeti safaris run with licensed operators. LGBTQ+ travelers: same-sex relations criminalized + advisory flags targeting - surface plainly. Re-verify each publish cycle.","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; SAFARI is the launch/demo SI - the park is primary safari (not globaladv); globaladv carries the balloon/walking add-ons; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"balloon + walking safari add-ons"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future","note":"Maasai"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Singita Grumeti / Namiri Plains - apex Serengeti stay","why_ultra":"private-concession luxury, exclusive game, butlered tented suites - the migration to yourself","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$2,000-4,000+/night"},{"name":"A private migration mobile camp + private guide + balloon","why_ultra":"exclusive-use mobile camp that moves with the herds, private vehicle/guide + the dawn balloon","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"A Northern-Circuit private-guided week (Serengeti + Ngorongoro + Tarangire)","why_ultra":"private guide + vehicle across the marquee parks, luxury camps throughout","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-31","hero":{"query":"Serengeti National Park, Tanzania"},"geo":{"lat":-2.3333,"lng":34.8333},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["lake-manyara-tanzania","ngorongoro-crater-tanzania","nyerere-selous-tanzania","ruaha-tanzania","tarangire-tanzania"]}'::jsonb, 1),
  ('volcanoes-national-park-rwanda', '05A', 'Volcanoes National Park', 'Rwanda', 'Gorillas in the mist', 'live', 'verified', 'safariGiraffe', 'Rwanda — Volcanoes / Virunga', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Rwanda''s flagship mountain-gorilla trek (the wow) in the Virunga volcanoes - a one-hour habituated-family encounter; world mountain-gorilla population now 1,063 (no longer critically endangered); the birthplace of African conservation (Dian Fossey/Karisoke 1967)","Permit $1,500/trekker (RDB), only 98/day, sells out - book 3-6 months ahead via a licensed operator or RDB (Irembo); min age 15; ~2h from Kigali - the accessible, premium gorilla trek","Also: golden-monkey trekking (bamboo), Mount Bisoke crater-lake hike (3,711m, most popular), Karisimbi summit (4,507m, Rwanda''s highest, 2-day), Dian Fossey grave hike, Kwita Izina gorilla-naming (Sep)","was) - bookable disclose+consent","gorilla trek = strenuous high-altitude (~2,500-3,700m) muddy rainforest hike (moderate fitness); trekking rules: 7m distance, mask, max 1hr, max 8/group, armed ranger, no trekking if ill","Sold via Rwandan safari DMCs 10-20% - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; the $1,500 RDB permit is non-commissionable pass-through; RWF (~1,467/USD); visa on arrival $30; malaria year-round (prophylaxis); AMREF for evac"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (police) / 912 ambulance / 111 fire; AMREF Flying Doctors for high-terrain evac","hospital":"Remote/high terrain - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Musanze/Kigali","malaria":"present year-round (chloroquine-resistant) - prophylaxis advised; DEET at dusk (lower at altitude but real)","yellow_fever":"required only if arriving from a YF-endemic country (not direct from the US)","activity_note":"Gorilla trek = strenuous high-altitude (~2,500-3,700m) muddy hike (moderate fitness); rules: 7m/1hr/mask/max 8/armed ranger/no trekking if ill. Volcano climbs = altitude sickness risk. Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda","read":"2026-09-04T12:02:55Z","page_updated":"2026-09-04T10:15:14+01:00","source_country":"rwanda","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"fcdo_zones":[{"name":"Within ~10 km of the DRC border","lvl":4,"except":["Volcanoes National Park"],"note":"Unrest. Multiple armed groups, individuals and military forces operate in North and South Kivu; violence may spill into Rwanda without warning. US government employees need special authorisation to travel here. State states Volcanoes National Park is not included in this area."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb (drier, firmer trails; permits sell out; Kwita Izina Sep spikes demand)","shoulder":"early Mar + late Nov (softer)","green":"Mar-May + Oct-Nov (rains - lush, muddier; 30% low-season permit discount Nov-May IF you also pre-book Akagera and/or Nyungwe nights)","booking_lead":"permits + luxury lodges 3-6 mo (Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb sell out; only 98 permits/day); green 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"the Nov-May 30%-off permit (with Akagera/Nyungwe nights) - sell a 3-park Rwanda circuit to unlock it","event_peaks":"Kwita Izina (Sep) + Christmas/NY + Jun-Sep dry","fire_date":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb 6-9 mo out; Nov-May discounted 3-park circuit by prior Aug-Sep"},"jewels":[{"name":"The mountain-gorilla trek","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$1,000-3,000+/pp/day (permit-inclusive)","timing":"year-round; Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb peak; book 3-6 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the single most moving hour in wildlife travel","si":"safari","blurb":"the single most moving hour in wildlife travel","when":"year-round; Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb peak; book 3-6 mo","commission":"DMC 10-20% (permit pass-through)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Kwita Izina - the gorilla-naming ceremony","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"event + trek","timing":"September","draw_rank":2,"hook":"Rwanda''s global conservation celebration each September — newborn gorillas named before thousands; a rare, meaningful event to time a trip around","si":"safari","blurb":"Rwanda''s global conservation celebration each September — newborn gorillas named before thousands; a rare, meaningful event to time a trip around","when":"September","commission":"DMC + event","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — commission lane ''dmc + event''","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","event"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Golden-monkey trekking","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$100/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the Virungas'' other primate — troops of endangered golden monkeys in the bamboo, a budget-friendlier, joyful half-day","si":"adventure","blurb":"the Virungas'' other primate — troops of endangered golden monkeys in the bamboo, a budget-friendlier, joyful half-day","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","commission":"DMC/RDB","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Mount Bisoke crater-lake hike + Karisimbi summit","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$75-400/pp","timing":"dry season; guided","draw_rank":2,"hook":"the park''s most popular hike to Bisoke''s crater lake, or the strenuous 2-day summit of Karisimbi — volcano-country adventure between gorilla days","si":"adventure","blurb":"the park''s most popular hike to Bisoke''s crater lake, or the strenuous 2-day summit of Karisimbi — volcano-country adventure between gorilla days","when":"dry season; guided","commission":"DMC/RDB","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The Dian Fossey grave hike (Karisoke)","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$75/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a pilgrimage through the forest to Fossey''s grave beside her gorilla Digit, at the site of the 1967 Karisoke Research Center","si":"deepdive","blurb":"a pilgrimage through the forest to Fossey''s grave beside her gorilla Digit, at the site of the 1967 Karisoke Research Center","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","commission":"DMC/RDB","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["deepdive"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A gorilla-lodge honeymoon (Singita / One&Only / Bisate)","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$1,500-5,000+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 3-6 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the Virungas'' apex lodges — Singita Kwitonda''s volcano-view suites, One&Only Gorilla''s Nest, Bisate''s cone-shaped villas — fireside luxury after the trek; honeymoon-grade","si":"ultra","blurb":"the Virungas'' apex lodges — Singita Kwitonda''s volcano-view suites, One&Only Gorilla''s Nest, Bisate''s cone-shaped villas — fireside luxury after the trek; honeymoon-grade","when":"standing; peak 3-6 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"destination","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Virunga honeymoon","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Volcanoes?","a":"The trek itself, and the altitude. The gorilla trek is a strenuous, high-altitude (~2,500-3,700m), often muddy rainforest hike — come with moderate fitness; malaria is year-round (prophylaxis + DEET), and it is remote — carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance. **FCDO travel advice for Rwanda:** the FCDO advises against all but essential travel to NAMED AREAS — parts of Rusizi District within 10km of the DRC border. *https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda — page updated 2026-06-10. Quoted unchanged; TravelWell does not state whether this destination lies inside a named area.*","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How much is the gorilla permit and how do I book it?","a":"US$1,500 per trekker, and with only 98 permits/day it sells out - book 3-6 months ahead through a licensed operator or the Rwanda Development Board (Irembo). Minimum age 15.","source":"volcanoesnationalpark.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How hard is the gorilla trek and what are the rules?","a":"Moderate-to-strenuous: 1-7 hours through steep, muddy, high-altitude forest to reach the family, then max 1 hour with them, 7 m minimum distance, a face mask, max 8 per group, an armed ranger, and no trekking if you''re ill. Porters are available and recommended.","source":"visitrwandagorilla.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Rwanda or Uganda for gorillas in 2026?","a":"Rwanda''s permit is pricier ($1,500 vs Uganda''s $800), and Volcanoes is 2 hours from Kigali. **FCDO travel advice:** for Rwanda the FCDO advises against all but essential travel to named areas (parts of Rusizi District within 10km of the DRC border) — *gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda, updated 2026-06-10*. For Uganda the FCDO names no advisory against travel — *gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda, updated 2026-07-27*. Read both before choosing; TravelWell states no preference on safety grounds.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit, and what else can I do?","a":"Best in the drier Jun-Sep and Dec-Feb; beyond the gorillas, track golden monkeys, hike Bisoke''s crater lake, climb Karisimbi, and make the Dian Fossey grave pilgrimage - a 2-3-day stay rewards.","source":"volcanoesparkrwanda.org","si_tag":"globaladv"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Volcanoes NP Rwanda Gorilla Trekking Guide: Permits, Fitness, Best Time & Safety","meta_description":"Plan a Volcanoes National Park gorilla trek - Rwanda''s flagship mountain-gorilla experience in the Virungas: the $1,500 permit and how to book it, the fitness and rules, Dian Fossey''s Karisoke, golden monkeys and volcano hikes, 2 hours from Kigali - with the FCDO advisory, altitude and health intel.","slug":"volcanoes-np-rwanda","primary_keyword":"Volcanoes National Park gorilla trekking","long_tail":["Rwanda gorilla permit cost 2026","gorilla trekking fitness Rwanda","Dian Fossey grave hike","golden monkey trekking Rwanda","Mount Bisoke hike","Rwanda vs Uganda gorillas","is Rwanda safe"],"search_language":"fr","local_keywords":["Parc National des Volcans","ingagi","Karisoke","Bisoke","Karisimbi","Kwita Izina","inguge z''izahabu"],"hreflang":["en","fr"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-01","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-01","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:58Z","source_updated":"2026-06-10T15:14:19+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["reconsider-travel","regional-ebola-alert"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"was). Re-verify each cycle.","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; SAFARI is the launch/demo SI - the mountain-gorilla trek is primary safari; golden monkeys + volcano hikes + Fossey grave hike = globaladv; Fossey/Karisoke conservation legacy = deepdive; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"mountain gorilla trekking"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"golden monkeys + Bisoke/Karisimbi volcano hikes + Dian Fossey grave hike"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"Singita/One&Only/Bisate/Sabyinyo"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"Dian Fossey / Karisoke"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Singita Kwitonda / One&Only Gorilla''s Nest - the Virungas'' apex stays","why_ultra":"volcano-view suites, private guiding + butlered luxury at the forest edge, the gorilla trek from the doorstep","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$2,500-5,000+/night"},{"name":"A private double-gorilla-permit + golden-monkey + Fossey week","why_ultra":"two gorilla treks (different families) + golden monkeys + the Fossey grave hike + a Bisoke climb, privately guided from an ultra lodge","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"A 3-park Rwanda circuit (Volcanoes + Akagera + Nyungwe)","why_ultra":"gorillas + Big-Five Akagera + Nyungwe chimps/canopy walk, private-guided - and it unlocks the Nov-May 30% permit discount","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Volcanoes National Park, Rwanda"},"geo":{"lat":-1.4667,"lng":29.5},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["akagera-np-rwanda","nyungwe-forest-rwanda"]}'::jsonb, 2)
insert into public.destinations (id, region_code, name, country, line, status, depth, img, sub_region, si, feel, tier_range, price_band, draw_rank, data, position) values
  ('lamu-island-kenya', '05A', 'Lamu Island', 'Kenya', 'Seven hundred years of Swahili stone, and no cars', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Kenya — Lamu Archipelago', '{"culture","deepdive","romance","tropical","ultra","family"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"safety":{"zone":"Lamu County","zone_except":"Lamu Island","notes":"FCDO advises against all travel to Lamu County, except for Lamu Island and Manda Island.","posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","verified":"2026-09-03","malaria":"high on the Kenyan coast, year-round","medevac":"by air, coordinated through AMREF","emergency":"999 / 112 · Kenya Red Cross 1199","fcdo":{"posture":"bookable_caution","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","authority_updated":"2026-09-01","read":"2026-09-03","quoted_verbatim":true,"alert_status":["avoid_all_travel_to_parts","avoid_all_but_essential_travel_to_parts"],"coverage_judgement":"NOT MADE — TravelWell does not state whether this destination lies inside or outside a named area. The FCDO''s own exception clause names Lamu Island and Manda Island; that is a fact about its text, not our judgement.","posture_note":"bookable_caution conforms to the existing vocabulary. The booking hold carried at ingest (2026-09-24) was lifted on David''s ruling of 2026-09-28: the hold was reasoned from the retired State Level 4, and the FCDO''s own exception clause names Lamu Island."}},"key_facts":["Lamu Old Town was inscribed by UNESCO in 2001 as the oldest and best-preserved Swahili settlement in East Africa, cited for its coral-stone buildings, inner courtyards, verandas and carved doors. Source: https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1055/ accessed 2026-06-29, V.","The island has no cars; transport is by dhow and by more than three thousand donkeys, including the transfer from the airstrip. Source: https://www.spiritedpursuit.com/blog/ultimate-guide-to-exploring-lamu-kenya accessed 2026-06-29, V.","Maulidi was developed in its Lamu form by al-Habib Swaleh in 1866 and runs four days of praise-poem recitals, music, dhow and donkey races and a zeffe parade. Source: https://lamu.go.ke/maulid-festival/ accessed 2026-06-29, V.","Maulidi falls in Rabi ul Awwal, the third month of the Islamic calendar, placing it around May-June in 2026, and moves roughly eleven days earlier each year. Source: https://www.exploriada.com/festivals/africa/kenya/maulid/ accessed 2026-09-03, V.","The Lamu Cultural Festival runs 30 November to 2 December 2026. Source: https://www.instagram.com/p/DWTFoVsiYFK/ accessed 2026-09-03, V.","Shela Beach runs roughly 12 km from Shela Village toward Kipungani, about a 45-minute beach walk or a 10-minute boat from town. Source: https://bestkenya.ke/blog/kenya-coast-guide/lamu-island-complete-guide accessed 2026-06-29, V.","Safarilink flies to Manda Airport (LAU) with seven nonstop flights a week from Malindi plus direct service to Nairobi; Manda sits about a mile from the town centre with no road link. Source: https://www.flightsfrom.com/LAU accessed 2026-09-03, V.","The Majlis on Manda Island offers private-island pool villas and a spa from KES 30,000+ per night, the only rate in this file and the property''s own published floor. Source: https://www.thehotelguru.com/best-hotels-in/kenya/lamu accessed 2026-09-03, est.","Commission hooks on an IATA/IATAN number and CLIA has essentially no African representation, so a CLIA-only agency needs a host''s IATA/IATAN or a DMC that accepts those affiliations. Source: https://www.foratravel.com/join/resources/travel-agent-commission accessed 2026-06-29, V.","The FCDO''s alert_status for Kenya is avoid_all_travel_to_parts and avoid_all_but_essential_travel_to_parts, with no numeric level; the FCDO publishes none for any country. Source: https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/kenya read 2026-09-03, V.","Malaria risk is high on the Kenyan coast and evacuation from the island is by air via AMREF. Source: https://wwwnc.cdc.gov/travel/yellowbook/2024/preparing/yellow-fever-vaccine-malaria-prevention-by-country/kenya accessed 2026-06-29, V."],"jewels":[{"name":"Lamu Old Town — UNESCO-listed 2001","si":"culture","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"The carved-door and courtyard houses","si":"culture","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"The car-free town — donkeys and dhows","si":"culture","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"The Lamu Cultural Festival","si":"culture","tier":"essential","commission":"operator-direct","when":"2026-11-30/2026-12-02"},{"name":"Seven centuries of continuous habitation","si":"deepdive","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Maulidi as Lamu made it","si":"deepdive","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"lunar — Rabi ul Awwal","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"The Swahili house form, with a guide","si":"deepdive","tier":"essential","commission":"operator-direct","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Peponi, Shela","si":"romance","tier":"premier","commission":"hotel-direct","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Forodhani House, Shela beach","si":"romance","tier":"premier","commission":"villa-direct","when":"year-round"},{"name":"The Shela beach walk","si":"romance","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Shela Beach — roughly 12 km of sand (Source: bestkenya.ke, V)","si":"tropical","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Dhow island-hopping","si":"tropical","tier":"comfort","commission":"operator-direct","when":"year-round"},{"name":"The Majlis, Manda Island","si":"ultra","tier":"ultra","commission":"none held","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Kizingoni Beach Houses","si":"family","tier":"comfort","commission":"villa-direct","when":"year-round"},{"name":"The donkeys — three thousand of them","si":"family","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why are there no cars on Lamu?","a":"The town predates them and its alleys are too narrow — transport is by donkey, of which there are more than three thousand, and by dhow.","source":"https://www.spiritedpursuit.com/blog/ultimate-guide-to-exploring-lamu-kenya","accessed":"2026-06-29"},{"q":"What is Lamu Old Town listed for?","a":"UNESCO inscribed it in 2001 as the oldest and best-preserved Swahili settlement in East Africa, citing its coral-stone buildings, inner courtyards, verandas and carved doors.","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1055/","accessed":"2026-06-29"},{"q":"When is the Maulidi festival?","a":"It falls in Rabi ul Awwal, the third month of the Islamic calendar, placing it around May to June in 2026, and it moves about eleven days earlier each year — so the dates must be confirmed for the year of travel rather than carried forward.","source":"https://www.exploriada.com/festivals/africa/kenya/maulid/","accessed":"2026-09-03"},{"q":"When is the Lamu Cultural Festival?","a":"30 November to 2 December 2026, over three days.","source":"https://www.instagram.com/p/DWTFoVsiYFK/","accessed":"2026-09-03"},{"q":"How do I get to Lamu?","a":"Fly to Manda Airport on Safarilink — seven nonstop flights a week from Malindi, plus service from Nairobi — then cross to the island by boat, as there is no road link.","source":"https://www.flightsfrom.com/LAU","accessed":"2026-09-03"},{"q":"What does the FCDO say about Lamu?","a":"The FCDO advises against all travel to a list of named areas in northern and eastern Kenya, and its wording for one of them reads \"Lamu County, except for Lamu Island and Manda Island.\" The full quoted text and the page''s own updated date are in the safety section, and travellers should read the FCDO''s page directly before booking.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","accessed":"2026-09-03"},{"q":"Is there a malaria risk?","a":"Malaria risk is high on the Kenyan coast, and this is a remote island where medical evacuation is by air — prophylaxis, evening bite protection and a travel-health consultation before departure are the planning items.","source":"https://wwwnc.cdc.gov/travel/yellowbook/2024/preparing/yellow-fever-vaccine-malaria-prevention-by-country/kenya","accessed":"2026-06-29"}]}'::jsonb, 3),
  ('diani-beach-kenya', '05A', 'Diani Beach', 'Kenya', 'Africa''s leading beach, with a safari up the road', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Kenya — South Coast / Diani', '{"tropical","diveglobal","ocean","romance","family","wellness","ultra"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"safety":{"source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","verified":"2026-09-03","malaria":"year-round coastal transmission risk","emergency":"999 / 112 · Kenya Red Cross 1199","fcdo":{"posture":"bookable_standard","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","authority_updated":"2026-09-01","read":"2026-09-03","quoted_verbatim":true,"coverage_judgement":"NOT MADE — TravelWell does not state whether this destination lies inside a named area"}},"key_facts":["The FCDO advises against all travel to named areas including Lamu County except for Lamu Island and Manda Island, and against all but essential travel to further named areas. TravelWell does not state whether this destination lies inside a named area. Source: gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya, FCDO page updated 2026-09-01, read 2026-09-03.","Roughly 25 km of white coral sand behind a fringing reef; repeatedly named Africa''s Leading Beach Destination at the World Travel Awards, whose 2024 Africa gala was held at Diani. Source: https://www.travelandtourworld.com/news/article/africas-best-tourism-destinations-and-leaders-shine-at-the-2024-world-travel-awards-in-diani-beach-kenya/ accessed 2026-06-29, V.","Diving the Crab, established 1985, is a PADI 5-star centre with 29 dive sites all within a 40-minute boat ride; whale sharks are seen November to February. Source: divingthecrab.com/diving-kenya, accessed 2026-09-03.","Two kite monsoons: Kusi June-September is the stronger season, Kaskazi December-February the lighter and the beginner window. Source: iksurfmag.com, accessed 2026-06-29.","Ukunda Airstrip (UKA/HKUK) serves Diani, Ukunda, Tiwi and Msambweni; six airlines operate, and the Nairobi route carries roughly 31 flights a week, 37% of all weekly departures. Source: flightsfrom.com/UKA and en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukunda_Airport, accessed 2026-09-03.","Alfajiri Villas is three private-use villas each with its own chef and butler; Almanara is nine villas plus a five-bedroom boutique hotel with personal chef and waiter service. Source: alfajirivillas.com and almanararesort.com, accessed 2026-09-03.","Colobus Conservation protects the endangered Angolan black-and-white colobus and runs the colobridge rope bridges over Diani Beach Road. Source: lonelyplanet.com Diani colobus centre, accessed 2026-06-29.","A dedicated always-staffed recompression chamber on the immediate south coast is NOT publicly confirmed; DAN Southern Africa''s 24-hour hotline +27 82 810 6010 coordinates the nearest available chamber. Source: dansa.org/chamber-network, accessed 2026-06-29.","The Kenyan coast carries year-round malaria transmission risk. Source: wwwnc.cdc.gov/travel/destinations/traveler/none/kenya, accessed 2026-06-29."],"jewels":[{"name":"The lagoon beach — roughly 25 km of coral sand (Source: travelandtourworld.com, V)","si":"tropical","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Diving the Crab — 29 sites within 40 minutes","si":"diveglobal","tier":"comfort","commission":"operator-direct","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Whale sharks off the reef","si":"diveglobal","tier":"comfort","commission":"operator-direct","when":"November-February"},{"name":"Funguo House Reef Wreck","si":"diveglobal","tier":"comfort","commission":"operator-direct","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Kaskazi kite season — the beginner wind","si":"ocean","tier":"comfort","commission":"operator-direct","when":"December-February"},{"name":"Kusi kite season — the advanced wind","si":"ocean","tier":"comfort","commission":"operator-direct","when":"June-September"},{"name":"Snorkelling the fringing reef","si":"ocean","tier":"essential","commission":"operator-direct","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Sunset dhow sail to the sandbank","si":"romance","tier":"comfort","commission":"operator-direct","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Colobus Conservation and the colobridges","si":"family","tier":"essential","commission":"none held","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Alfajiri Villas — three private-use villas","si":"ultra","tier":"ultra","commission":"none held","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Almanara Luxury Boutique Hotel & Villas","si":"ultra","tier":"luxury","commission":"none held","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Leopard Beach Resort & Spa","si":"wellness","tier":"premier","commission":"bed-bank (Bedsonline/HBX, WebBeds)","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Baobab Beach Resort & Spa","si":"wellness","tier":"comfort","commission":"bed-bank (Bedsonline/HBX, WebBeds)","when":"year-round"},{"name":"The reef-protected lagoon for small children","si":"family","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Beach-and-bush combine out of Ukunda (UKA)","si":"family","tier":"premier","commission":"bed-bank + air, agent-assembled","when":"year-round"},{"name":"Africa''s Leading Beach Destination — the award strip","si":"tropical","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"},{"name":"Low-tide sandbank walk to the reef","si":"tropical","tier":null,"commission":"none held","when":"year-round","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is whale shark season at Diani Beach?","a":"November through February is the window the dive operators publish for whale shark encounters here.","source":"https://www.divingthecrab.com/diving-kenya/","accessed":"2026-09-03"},{"q":"How many dive sites are there, and how far out?","a":"Twenty-nine sites, all within a forty-minute boat ride, with dolphins a frequent sighting on the way.","source":"https://www.divingthecrab.com/diving-kenya/","accessed":"2026-09-03"},{"q":"Which kite season suits a beginner?","a":"Kaskazi, December to February, is the lighter of the two monsoons; Kusi, June to September, is stronger and suits an experienced rider.","source":"https://www.iksurfmag.com/travel-guides/africa/kenya/diani-beach/","accessed":"2026-06-29"},{"q":"Is there a recompression chamber nearby?","a":"A dedicated always-staffed chamber on the immediate south coast is not publicly confirmed. The DAN Southern Africa 24-hour hotline, +27 82 810 6010, coordinates the nearest available chamber and evacuation, and the current nearest operational chamber should be verified with the dive operator at the time of travel.","source":"https://www.dansa.org/chamber-network","accessed":"2026-06-29"},{"q":"Do I need malaria precautions?","a":"The Kenyan coast carries year-round malaria transmission risk; prophylaxis and evening bite protection are the standard planning items, and a travel-health consultation before departure is the route to a current recommendation.","source":"https://wwwnc.cdc.gov/travel/destinations/traveler/none/kenya","accessed":"2026-06-29"},{"q":"How do I combine Diani with a safari?","a":"Ukunda Airstrip is ten to fifteen minutes from the resorts and runs roughly 31 flights a week to Nairobi, which is the connection most beach-and-bush itineraries are built on.","source":"https://www.flightsfrom.com/UKA","accessed":"2026-09-03"}]}'::jsonb, 4),
  ('akagera-np-rwanda', '05A', 'Akagera National Park', 'Rwanda', 'Rwanda''s Big Five comeback', 'live', 'verified', 'elephant', 'Rwanda — Akagera', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Rwanda''s only Big-Five savanna park + one of conservation''s great turnarounds - African Parks (with the RDB since 2010) reintroduced lions (2015), black rhinos (2017), and southern white rhinos in 2021 (30) and 2025 (70, ''Rhino Rewild'')","~1,100 km2 of plains, hills and lakes (largest protected wetland in central/eastern Africa); Big Five game drives + Lake Ihema boat safari (hippos, crocs, ~550 birds incl. the shoebill) + night drives","Uncrowded (NatGeo Best of the World 2026) and ~2 hours from Kigali - fly in the morning, game-drive by lunch; completes the 3-park Rwanda circuit with Volcanoes (gorillas) + Nyungwe (chimps)","disclose + consent","Fees 2026: $100/adult, $50/child; sleeping in-park halves the fee nights 2-3 and is FREE from night 4 (up to a week) - a real reason to stay; best Jun-Sep + Jan-Feb","Sold via Rwandan safari DMCs 10-15% - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; African Parks fees bundle/pass-through; RWF (~1,467/USD); visa on arrival $30; malaria year-round in the lowland east; AMREF for evac"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (police) / 912 ambulance / 111 fire; AMREF Flying Doctors for bush evac","hospital":"Remote (~2h from Kigali) - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Kigali","malaria":"present year-round in the lowland east (chloroquine-resistant) - prophylaxis advised; DEET at dawn/dusk","yellow_fever":"required only if arriving from a YF-endemic country (not direct from the US)","activity_note":"Dangerous game at close range - stay in the vehicle, follow the guide, never approach rhino. Lake Ihema boat safari: hippo pods + shoreline crocs - remain seated, limbs in the boat. Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda","read":"2026-09-04T12:02:55Z","page_updated":"2026-09-04T10:15:14+01:00","source_country":"rwanda","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"fcdo_zones":[{"name":"Within ~10 km of the DRC border","lvl":4,"except":["Volcanoes National Park"],"note":"Unrest. Multiple armed groups, individuals and military forces operate in North and South Kivu; violence may spill into Rwanda without warning. US government employees need special authorisation to travel here. State states Volcanoes National Park is not included in this area."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Sep (esp Jul-Aug, dry, wildlife at water) + Dec holiday","shoulder":"Oct-Nov + Mar (softer rates, good game)","green":"Jan-early Feb (fewer vehicles, lower lodge rates) + Apr-May (long rains, lush, cheapest)","booking_lead":"lodges (few, small) 2-5 mo for Jun-Sep; in-park stay-longer fee break (nights 2-3 half, 4+ free) rewards multi-night; green 1-2 mo","off_season_specials":"Jan-Feb + Apr-May value; the 3-park Rwanda circuit (Volcanoes + Nyungwe + Akagera) unlocks the Nov-May 30% gorilla-permit discount","event_peaks":"Jul-Aug + Christmas/NY; N-Hemisphere summer","fire_date":"Jun-Sep 4-6 mo out; 3-park circuit (with the gorilla discount) by prior Aug-Sep; position as quiet accessible Big-Five vs crowded Serengeti/Mara"},"jewels":[{"name":"A Big-Five game drive (the comeback)","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~$400-1,800/pp/day","timing":"Jun-Sep + Jan-Feb; dry best","draw_rank":1,"hook":"lion, black + white rhino, elephant, buffalo and leopard on rewilded plains — one of Africa''s great conservation success stories, with hardly another vehicle","si":"safari","blurb":"lion, black + white rhino, elephant, buffalo and leopard on rewilded plains — one of Africa''s great conservation success stories, with hardly another vehicle","when":"Jun-Sep + Jan-Feb; dry best","commission":"safari DMC 10-15%","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Rhino tracking","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"within the safari","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"both black rhino and southern white rhino — Akagera is now one of the more reliable rhino parks in East Africa, guide-radio-coordinated","si":"safari","blurb":"both black rhino and southern white rhino — Akagera is now one of the more reliable rhino parks in East Africa, guide-radio-coordinated","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"safari DMC 10-15%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"The Lake Ihema boat safari","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$40-50/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"large hippo pods + shoreline Nile crocodiles are the leading on-water hazards — remain seated, keep limbs in the boat","si":"adventure","blurb":"large hippo pods + shoreline Nile crocodiles are the leading on-water hazards — remain seated, keep limbs in the boat","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"DMC/park","wells":["activities","move"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A night drive","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$40-60/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the nocturnal cast — leopard, hyena, bushbaby, genet — on a guided after-dark drive, an experience the day misses","si":"adventure","blurb":"the nocturnal cast — leopard, hyena, bushbaby, genet — on a guided after-dark drive, an experience the day misses","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"DMC/park","wells":["stay","move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The African Parks conservation story","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the rewilding of Akagera — from war-emptied to full Big Five under African Parks + the RDB, with the \"Rhino Rewild\" translocations","si":"deepdive","blurb":"the rewilding of Akagera — from war-emptied to full Big Five under African Parks + the RDB, with the \"Rhino Rewild\" translocations","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"park/DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — commission lane ''park/dmc''","si_all":["deepdive","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Magashi Camp honeymoon","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$800-2,500+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 2-5 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Wilderness''s tented lakeside camp on a game-rich peninsula — private guiding, boat safaris and Big Five from the doorstep","si":"ultra","blurb":"Wilderness''s tented lakeside camp on a game-rich peninsula — private guiding, boat safaris and Big Five from the doorstep","when":"standing; peak 2-5 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["activities","move","stay"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["romance","safari","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"An Akagera lakeside honeymoon","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Akagera?","a":"Dangerous game and the lake, plus the health advisory - not crime. Free-ranging lion, elephant and rhino at close range - stay in the vehicle and follow your guide; on the Lake Ihema boat safari keep seated among the hippo pods and shoreline crocs. Malaria is year-round in the lowland east (prophylaxis + DEET), and it''s remote - carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Akagera a real Big Five park?","a":"Yes - thanks to one of conservation''s great turnarounds. African Parks (managing with the RDB since 2010) brought back lions (2015) and rhinos (2017), and added white rhinos in 2021 and 2025 - restoring the full Big Five to a park that civil war had emptied.","source":"nationalgeographic.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Akagera?","a":"Jun-Sep and Jan-Feb (dry) - the bush thins, wildlife concentrates at water, and roads stay passable. Jan-early Feb is low season (fewer vehicles, lower lodge rates); the green rains bring lush scenery and birding.","source":"safaribookings.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How does Akagera fit a Rwanda trip, and is it worth it?","a":"Very much: Akagera is ~2 hours from Kigali, so it pairs naturally with the gorillas of Volcanoes and the chimps of Nyungwe into a 3-park Rwanda circuit - and staying in the park (nights 2-3 half-price, night 4+ free) rewards a longer stop.","source":"nationalgeographic.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Rwanda?","a":"Visa on arrival $30 (or online via Irembo); passport valid 6 months. Yellow fever is required only if arriving from a YF-endemic country (not direct from the US).","source":"thingstodoinrwanda.com","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Akagera Safari Guide: Rwanda''s Big Five Comeback, Lake Ihema Boat Safari, Fees & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan an Akagera safari - Rwanda''s Big-Five savanna comeback under African Parks (lions, black + white rhinos rewilded), a Lake Ihema boat safari for hippos, crocs and the shoebill, uncrowded and 2 hours from Kigali - with real safety, timing, fees and the 3-park Rwanda circuit.","slug":"akagera-np-rwanda","primary_keyword":"Akagera National Park safari","long_tail":["Akagera Big Five Rwanda","Akagera boat safari Lake Ihema","Akagera rhino reintroduction","Akagera park fees 2026","Rwanda safari and gorillas","is Akagera safe","Akagera vs Serengeti"],"search_la